  "description": "The intended audience is individuals who may be exposed to antisemitic tropes or who are susceptible to harmful stereotypes about Jewish communities, particularly those who might be influenced by or reinforce the idea that Jewish people are a burden on society or require special, segregated treatment. The meme targets viewers who may not recognize the hateful nature of the message or who may be predisposed to antisemitic views, using the visual of vulnerable Jewish children to evoke sympathy while simultaneously suggesting they are an 'extra' or 'problematic' group needing exclusion from normal societal structures.",
